  "summary_md": "A sharp split runs through today’s 30 Communication Equipment and Specialty Industrial Machinery names: defense, AI data-center, and 5G infrastructure spending are fueling record backlogs and rapid pivots, while a few legacy hardware stories face severe structural contraction. Laser Photonics (LASE) and Frequency Electronics (FEIM) ride anti-drone and space-defense tailwinds with contract wins, whereas Franklin Wireless (FKWL) is navigating a product-cycle collapse. Transformational bets define the day—Broadwind (BWEN) exited wind towers entirely, Inseego (INSG) awaits its Nokia acquisition to reshape its global footprint, and Amplitech (AMPG) turned R&D into commercial 5G certifications. Capital allocation signals are equally divergent: buybacks at Clearfield (CLFD) and margin-first repositioning at NETGEAR (NTGR) contrast with equity raises at Lantronix (LTRX) and acute liquidity pressure at Clean Energy Technologies (CETY). The common thread is a scramble to channel balance sheets and product lines toward high-visibility defense, AI fiber, and electrification contracts, with regulatory approvals acting as critical gatekeepers.",
